36,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":60.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.08662801250384944,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":62.2,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.31915753455252127,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03844035048124177,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":53.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.005265712825909041,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":56.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008270938533867317,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.00819,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Caesars Entertainment, Inc. operates as a gaming and hospitality company. It owns, leases, brands, or manages domestic properties in 18 states with slot machines, video lottery terminals and e-tables, and hotel rooms, as well as table games, including poker. The company also operates and conducts online gaming, retail and online sports wagering across 42 jurisdictions in North America, and iGaming in five jurisdictions in North America; sports betting from retail and online sportsbooks; and other games, such as keno. In addition, it operates casinos, dining venues, bars, nightclubs, lounges, hotels, and entertainment venues; and provides staffing and management services. In addition, the company operates as a real estate leasing company, that constructs and develops the Grand Bazaar. The company was founded in 1937 and is based in Reno, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas Robert Reeg CFA | CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 50K people. Revenue per employee of $230K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 35%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 23\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Caesars Entertainment, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $6.0B market cap on $11.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +32% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $497M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.155145929339479},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $18.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 88% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Wider Losses At Caesars Entertainment (CZR) Have Changed Its Investment Story","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nasdaq-czr/caesars-entertainment/news/how-wider-losses-at-caesars-entertainment-czr-have-changed-i","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793690778.125,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bid Pulled: Which Way Now for CZR Resources (ASX:CZR)?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/commodity/iron-ore/bid-pulled-which-way-now-for-czr-reso